From d8a7643131431b73622aa222c559ee2ce1df9a01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z0cal <gabriel_zocal@hotmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:25:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] EvalMod: degree-27 tables behind FIDESLIB_BTS_EVALMOD
 (bts.evalmod)

The shipped tables (FIDESlib degree 14 / degree 20, 5 double angles, 10 levels) are the default again, so the
records' plans, the Prefill-128 one and the oracle tests are as before. `bts.evalmod = "d27"` (runtime line
FIDESLIB_BTS_EVALMOD=d27) runs the degree-27 tables with 4 double angles (9 levels) on every route: pc-core
`EvalMod` names the tables, double angles and levels; the GPU setups (dense, StC-first, SparseB, classic) take
them from the Config, and the landings the compiler, the runtime/fakecap Shadows and the capture's fakecap use are
derived from `EvalMod::levels` (`BtsConfig::shift_evalmod`, `multi_stage_landing(.., em)`): every route but SPRU
lands one level shallower. The field is load-bearing (it binds the plan). pc-bench / pc-check read
FIDESLIB_BTS_EVALMOD from the environment. em_depth lists both series with their own double angles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
